 A non-zero exit means the service is down. Fail fast and report it, because a retry cannot help.
 
+## Retry or fail fast
+
+```dot
+digraph retry_or_fail_fast {
+    "Request failed or timed out" [shape=ellipse];
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" [shape=plaintext];
+    "Health check exited 0?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Fail fast and report the service is down" [shape=box];
+    "Response is 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Fail fast and fix the request" [shape=box];
+    "Is the request a POST?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [shape=octagon, style=filled, fillcolor=red, fontcolor=white];
+    "Fail fast and report the failure" [shape=box];
+    "Retry with the same key" [shape=box];
+    "Retry up to 3 times, after 1 s, 2 s and 4 s" [shape=box];
+
+    "Request failed or timed out" -> "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health";
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" -> "Health check exited 0?";
+    "Health check exited 0?" -> "Fail fast and report the service is down" [label="no"];
+    "Health check exited 0?" -> "Response is 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" [label="yes"];
+    "Response is 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" -> "Fail fast and fix the request" [label="yes"];
+    "Response is 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" -> "Is the request a POST?" [label="no"];
+    "Is the request a POST?" -> "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the request a POST?" -> "Retry up to 3 times, after 1 s, 2 s and 4 s" [label="no"];
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Retry with the same key" [label="yes"];
+    "Has an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [label="no, even on a timeout or 503"];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" -> "Fail fast and report the failure";
+}
+```
